.TH ORO-BACKGROUND 3 "" "Oro Runtime" "Oro Runtime API Manual"
.SH NAME
oro:background \- JavaScript API module
.SH SYNOPSIS
.nf
import * as module from 'oro:background'
.fi
.SH DESCRIPTION
.PP
Explicit native durable tasks. Android supports expired share\-cache cleanup; arbitrary JavaScript, deferred sync and unattended push are not implemented.
.SH REFERENCE
.TP
\fBregister(taskKind)\fR
Checks the supported native task kind. This does not register a JS handler or authorize future application work. Other platforms reject with ENOSYS.
\fBParameters:\fR
.br
\fItaskKind\fR (\&'share\-prune'; required)
\fBReturns:\fR
.br
\fIPromise<BackgroundTaskSupport>\fR
.TP
\fBschedule(options)\fR
Schedules one unique, persisted Android share\-prune job. Scheduling replaces the previous cleanup of that kind. Android decides timing and boot recovery; force\-stop prevents execution until relaunch. The task removes only expired runtime\-owned share files; it never executes JS, contacts servers, or retries application mutations. Failed native cleanup has at most three attempts with Android exponential backoff starting at 30 seconds. Requires background.enabled.
\fBParameters:\fR
.br
\fIoptions\fR (BackgroundScheduleOptions; required)
\fBReturns:\fR
.br
\fIPromise<BackgroundTaskState>\fR
.TP
\fBcancel(taskKind)\fR
Cancels the unique native cleanup. A running deletion may finish its current file before observing cancellation. Already removed expired files stay removed.
\fBParameters:\fR
.br
\fItaskKind\fR (\&'share\-prune'; optional; default 'share\-prune')
\fBReturns:\fR
.br
\fIPromise<BackgroundTaskState>\fR
.TP
\fBstatus(taskKind)\fR
Reads actual native scheduling availability and durable state. An interrupted record with no retained OS job is explicit; it is not silently re\-enqueued. Other platforms reject with ENOSYS.
\fBParameters:\fR
.br
\fItaskKind\fR (\&'share\-prune'; optional; default 'share\-prune')
\fBReturns:\fR
.br
\fIPromise<BackgroundTaskStatus>\fR
.TP
\fBavailable\fR
Whether this document requested the native Android cleanup capability. Read status() for actual manifest and scheduler availability.
.TP
\fBbackground\fR
Documented variable exposed by this module.
